uld have been one of the restaurant sector's largest-ever deals. Bloomberg's Redd Brown joins to...\n\n12 days ago - Bloomberg Markets and Finance\n\n### Starbucks says not buying Chipotle, ends takeover speculation\n\nStarbucks (SBUX.O), opens new tab is not buying Chipotle Mexican Grill (CMG.N), opens new tab, the ​coffee chain said on Monday, quashing talk of a deal that could have been the largest-ever involving...\n\n12 days ago - Reuters\n\n### Starbucks says it is not buying Chipotle after takeover speculation\n\n\"Starbucks is not buying Chipotle,\" a Starbucks spokesperson told CNBC. The denial follows days of rumors that Starbucks was trying to acquire the fast-casual chain.\n\n12 days ago - CNBC\n\n### Is a Starbucks-Chipotle Merger Actually Possible?\n\nCould Starbucks really buy Chipotle? Restaurant analyst John Tower tells Yahoo Finance Executive Editor Brian Sozzi a deal is highly unlikely, but he won't rule it out, given CEO Brian Niccol's histor...\n\n14 days ago - Yahoo Finance\n\n### OpenAI's revenue scare, Delta earnings, what investors think of a Starbucks-Chipotle deal and more in Morning Squawk\n\nHere are five key things investors need to know to start the trading day.\n\n15 days ago - CNBC\n\n### Feel like a pumpkin-spice burrito? Analysts try to wrap their heads around a possible Starbucks-Chipotle tie-up.\n\nStarbucks investors would likely not be happy about the company adding debt to finance a deal to buy Chipotle, given that it already has a high debt load.\n\n16 days ago - Market Watch\n\n### Chipotle Jumps on Report of Potential Starbucks Takeover | Closing Bell\n\nComprehensive cross-platform coverage of the U.S. market close on Bloomberg Television, Bloomberg Radio, and YouTube with Romaine Bostick, Jess Menton, Carol Massar and Stacey Vanek Smith.\n\n16 days ago - Bloomberg Markets and Finance\n\n### Why a Starbucks takeover of Chipotle would — and wouldn't — make sense for both companies\n\nStarbucks has been working with advisers